# A slow taper keeps the light in the fundamental mode; a fast one scatters it into higher modes.
# Reference: the same propagation stepped independently in NumPy. The pipeline checks that transmission rises with length.
title Taper from 0.5 to 3 um over 20 um
reference 2.75
window width=20 length=40
guide straight x=0 width=0.5 from=0 to=10
guide taper x=0 w0=0.5 w1=3 from=10 to=30
guide straight x=0 width=3 from=30 to=40
launch mode x=0 width=0.5
monitor out z=40 x=0 width=3
plane end z=40
expect power out 0.991000039 2e-7
expect total end 0.999950250 2e-7
expect centroid end 0.0000000 2e-6
expect radius end 1.1671344 2e-6
expect neff 2.769133761 2e-8
